WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:03.960
So we're at the start of what's probably going
to be a very interesting week and there are

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:08.879
compelling things and funny things going on,
one that's funny is funny not because Joe

00:00:08.879 --> 00:00:13.639
Biden is the be all end all of fixing America
or anything like it.

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:19.190
But it's funny because it's a sign of just
how terribly the Republican Party has performed,

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:23.689
even for many Republicans over the last 18
months.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:32.070
Joe Biden's approval rating in Texas among
Texas voters is higher than Texas.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:36.070
His own Republican governor, Greg Abbott.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:43.320
If you can imagine, the poll conducted by
the University of Houston Hobby School of

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:51.230
Public Affairs has Joe Biden at a 41 percent
approval rating in Texas, whereas the Republican

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:56.870
governor, Greg Abbott, is only at 39 percent
approval in the state of Texas.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:59.550
Now, there's a bunch of interesting layers
to this story.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:03.490
And I hope to get get to all of them or at
least all that I'm aware of.

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:07.400
The first is that Greg Abbott is going to
be up for reelection in the year twenty, twenty

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.460
two.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.610
And there's talk of, better or worse, challenging
him.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:16.240
We saw Texas closer in the November of 2012
presidential election than it's been in a

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.130
very long time.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:23.660
And if these numbers remain where Joe Biden
is more popular than Greg Abbott in Texas,

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:27.870
it could be a really tough reelection and
it could be an opportunity for a Democratic

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.060
governor to actually win the state of Texas.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:33.140
That would be fascinating to see now.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:40.229
Second, this confirms that the high approval
that Joe Biden is experiencing nationally,

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:45.930
we saw it at 63 percent early last week or
the week before that is being supported not

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:51.370
just by Democratic approval of Joe Biden in
blue states, but it's also being supported

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:57.450
by higher than typical approval for a Democratic
president from voters in red states, including

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.720
the state of Texas.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:05.420
And then the third aspect of this is that
right now, at least much of what Biden has

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:10.749
done and much of what his approval is riding
on is his coronavirus response.

00:02:10.749 --> 00:02:17.180
I've been saying for weeks now, just move
forward with the one point nine trillion covid

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:20.819
relief package that's been proposed by Biden
and by Democrats.

00:02:20.819 --> 00:02:23.409
Don't negotiate with these bad faith Republicans.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.390
Let them all vote against it if that's what
they want to do.

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:28.659
And so far, Democrats are moving in that direction.

00:02:28.659 --> 00:02:34.349
The approval numbers for Biden overall and
uncovered response and the support of the

00:02:34.349 --> 00:02:40.859
covid relief bill to me signal that Republicans
are voting against the bill at their own peril,

00:02:40.859 --> 00:02:41.859
if that's what they do.

00:02:41.859 --> 00:02:48.139
What I mean by that is this covid relief bill
that Joe Biden and Democrats want is popular

00:02:48.139 --> 00:02:53.169
enough with Republicans that if Republican
senators and members of Congress all want

00:02:53.169 --> 00:02:57.219
to oppose it, they are taking on significant
political risk for doing so.

00:02:57.219 --> 00:03:00.499
Now, one important caveat about Abbott's approval.

00:03:00.499 --> 00:03:06.189
Some Republicans in Texas don't like Greg
Abbott because he did do a mask mandate.

00:03:06.189 --> 00:03:12.340
So it's not all as simple as Biden has a higher
approval because Abbott didn't do enough.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.559
There are people upset with Abbott in Texas
because he didn't do enough.

00:03:15.559 --> 00:03:18.840
And there are people upset with Abbott because
he did too much, even though he did a massive

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.840
mandate.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.269
It was basically toothless.

00:03:21.269 --> 00:03:23.719
And it's sort of like the worst of both worlds.

00:03:23.719 --> 00:03:28.919
But the point here is that even in Texas,
Joe Biden's approval higher than Republican

00:03:28.919 --> 00:03:33.530
Republican Governor Greg Abbott's, and that's
more evidence that the country is crossing

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:38.199
party lines on what they want to see as far
as covid response is concerned.

00:03:38.199 --> 00:03:43.290
And if Republicans become attached to we stood
in the way of covid.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:47.499
And we stood in the way of you getting any
money, it could continue to massacre them

00:03:47.499 --> 00:03:51.669
into 20, 22, and remember that under Donald
Trump, Republicans lost the House in twenty

00:03:51.669 --> 00:03:52.790
eighteen.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.180
They lost the Senate and the White House.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:55.529
In twenty twenty.

00:03:55.529 --> 00:04:01.730
They saw Georgia go blue and Texas go closer
to blue in the presidential election.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:07.180
And the Republican Party really is at risk
here and especially now with Donald Trump

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.500
considering launching this new political party.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.969
It is a very tender situation for the party.

00:04:12.969 --> 00:04:18.680
We'll talk a little bit more later about the
willingness of the Republican electorate to

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:20.949
abandon the party and to go with Trump.

00:04:20.949 --> 00:04:23.840
We have some new polling about that.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:27.870
But as has been the theme with the Republican
Party for the last four years, much of this

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.900
is unforced errors.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:37.139
This all goes back to if Trump had just let
Foushee run the show, had gotten behind guidelines,

00:04:37.139 --> 00:04:43.370
had offered American flag masks for Republicans
to buy and where he would have been reelected,

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:45.120
Republicans would probably still have the
Senate.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:49.919
Now we're talking about a Democratic president
with a higher approval rating in Texas than

00:04:49.919 --> 00:04:51.060
the Republican governor.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:51.930
Unbelievable stuff.

